i believe that no fight in the history  of one piece has been discussed as  heatedly by fans as the battle between  luffy and katakuri during the climax of  the whole cake island arc  while on the surface it seemed to be  similar to the usual pattern that  luffy's battle followed throughout the  story this one felt oddly but pleasantly  different and i think many people  couldn't quite pinpoint what exactly it  was that made category so unique as a  major one-piece antagonist compared to  the likes of crocodile luci or doe  flamingo  when we first meet category in the story  he's introduced as a typical trope of  the cool calm and competent villain that  seems to be on top of things no matter  what  compared to most of his siblings he  stands out as someone who's actually  able to take action on his own and we  understand right from the get-go that  this is someone who's essential in  keeping the big mom pirates relevant as  a yonko crew functioning as the de facto  captain during big mom's rage combined  with his power as well as the deep care  he shows for his family he's one of the  most popular members of the crew in all  of whole cake islands  on top of all this katakuri also  introduces us to the concept of future  sites a very advanced form of ken buncho  kohaki that allows him to look several  seconds ahead into the future and react  accordingly a skill so rare that it's  not even shared by his mother big mom  and so overall when luffy manages to  pull category into a one versus one  fight in the mirror world to enable his  crew's escape naturally we all  anticipated this battle to be one of the  most challenging ones for luffy so far  against an antagonist that seems  extremely rational and calculated  and what follows is one of the best  battles and character arcs in the story  so far  [Music]  this is where the main theme of  category's character comes into play and  it's actually so important that it will  serve as the overarching framework for  this entire character analysis  mirrors  everything about category is reflected  in the symbol of the mirror on the  smallest level this can be seen in terms  of his future size that is all about  looking ahead and seeing things that you  usually can't just like you can use a  mirror to look around corners  and just like a mirror your future side  can be blurred when losing composure  but i honestly think it's so much more  interesting to look at this symbol on a  much larger scale because the main  implication here is that katakuri and  luffy mirror each other as characters on  more than just one level  to really understand to what extent oda  has created katakuri as a mirrored  version of luffy i think it's best to  peel away the layers one by one  on the most superficial level luffy and  category are similar simply based on the  devil food powers  while luffy is made of rubber katakuri  is made of mochi a malleable sort of  rice cake that can easily change its  shape  this is not the first time that oda has  shown us a villain with a similar power  to luffy's  thinking back to before the time skip  bellamy was also quite similar to  luffy's ability in terms of speed and  bounciness  the purpose of this trope is to have the  protagonist quote unquote fight and  overcome himself and thus give us an  idea where he stands in terms of his  power developments  in bellamy's case we saw that luffy was  actually way stronger than him which was  in line with his up and coming rookie  status before the alabasta arc  katakuri however shows us the exact  opposite  while his powers are even more similar  to luffy's his message at the beginning  of the fight is clear  whatever you can do with your devil  fruit i can do better and so we learn  very quickly that the underlying subtext  of this battle is for luffy to overcome  himself and increase his fighting  abilities  in other words this was the very first  battle where in line with rayleigh's  explanation on ruskina he will have to  become stronger during a battle compared  to training beforehand as he did for  instance against lucci  and what makes this battle against  category so unique from luffy's  perspective is the incentive for it  you see in almost every single major  battle luffy's victory ends in the  liberation of the people oppressed by  the villain as he's fighting for their  sake in the first place  luffy defeating arlung for instance  meant freeing nami and her village from  his oppression  taking out crocodile meant the end of  the civil war and suffering in alabasta  and when luffy punched doflamingo down  into the ground it literally cut the  strings that were controlling dressrosa  it's this pattern that usually makes his  fight so satisfying to see  against katakuri however luffy doesn't  free whole cake island or the big mom  pirates from the yonkos rage and tyranny  [Music]  beating katakuri wouldn't change the  country itself  and since luffy has already retrieved  sanji and protected his crew by shutting  himself together with katakuri in the  mirror worlds there was no one to  liberate or rescue and so suddenly his  battle and relationship with katakuri  moved to a much more personal level that  was all about power and ideology and for  the very first time he was able to fully  focus on himself and his own ambitions  this is i think what makes katakuri so  different and unique in the story  [Music]  so here we have the main objective for  luffy however moving down yet another  layer luffy and katakuri mirror each  other not only on a physical level but  on a personal level as well  [Music]  and this is where we get to the really  interesting part of this video  as we slowly learn over the course of  their fight katakuri's cool and composed  demeanor starts to crack and slowly fall  apart  both him and luffy have crazily similar  personalities only that katakuri has  built up this false persona over time in  hope to protect his family  in his flashback we see a happy and  careless boy that is unapologetic about  who he is  when perospero tells him that his life  would be much easier if he simply  covered up his mouth katakuri answers  that he doesn't care what others think  about him and that he would simply beat  up anyone if necessary  [Music]  the second trait we notice about him is  his strong protective nature when it  comes to his family  this strongly reminds us of the luffy  that we know today and so he only adopts  his quote-unquote perfect persona once  brulee gets attacked because of him  he lost his true self to the desire to  protect his family we actually saw a  similar moment in luffy's life after  aces death where he lost faith in  himself  luckily however he had jinbe in that  moment to set him straight  unfortunately for katakuri though he  didn't have someone like that within the  ranks of his big but quite unloving  family  therefore he adopted this new persona to  protect his loved ones and we can also  see this discrepancy really well during  the merienda scene  [Music]  while luffy doesn't care looking weak in  front of his friends as we see in his  encounter with sanji earlier in this arc  nor about showing happiness and  enjoyment katakuri literally puts walls  around him to keep anyone from seeing  his love for lying down and eating  donuts  luffy has to break down those literal  walls for him to wake him up to the  loneliness he's in  despite being a well-respected member of  the biggest family in the world  nobody understands him and knows who he  really is at heart  and so i believe what really sparked  category's interest and initial anger  when facing off against luffy was the  fact that he saw himself and his lost  potential reflected in him and so he had  to prove to himself that he made the  right decision in hiding his true self  and covering up his face  thus at the beginning of the fight the  emphasis wasn't so much on i'm stronger  than you  but rather on everything you do i do  better  i believe that the excuse that luffy  will become a danger to big mom that  needs to be eliminated right away was  only part of his motivation  and so the fight became much more  personal for category as well  as a result we have a battle between two  people who are incredibly involved with  each other one fighting to reach his  potential in terms of power and the  other in terms of character  and i think that the resilience and will  that luffy demonstrates to ultimately  beat category are also wonderfully  reflected by the similar devil fruit  powers as well  while katakuri is mochi that when  pounded stays pretty much as it is luffy  being rubber always bounces back and  can't be squashed  this fantastic thematic concept combined  with a compelling multi-layered  personality  is what gives katakuri's character this  intimate and likable feel that is quite  unique in the story so far  both luffy and katakuri make the other  reflect on themselves and their  respective weaknesses  as a result the battle is one of the  best sequences of character crafting and  character development at the same time  mixing great physical growth on luffy's  part with great psychological growth on  categories  as their fight progresses katakuri gains  more and more respect for luffy  this is evident in the shift of language  used as karakori now is saying things  like  [Music]  [Music]  and so he slowly starts to admire  luffy's resilience and a rapid  development of his future side skills  it reaches a point where both are  fighting at full strength but both also  seem to be really enjoying their duel  this becomes especially clear in the  iconic scene where katakuri stabs  himself to make up for the wound he  inflicted to luffy after flampay's  interference  the fact that both of them take her and  the other onlookers out of the picture  with their congress hockey makes the  relationship between the two even better  in my opinion  at this point luffy has fully convinced  category that being yourself and living  authentically is important  not only for your own happiness and  growth but also for that of the people  around you  better to be understood and accepted by  few like brulee  rather than being admired for pretending  to be someone else by someone like  flampay  [Music]  katakuri throws up his scarf and starts  embracing his true self once again and  so while both fight at full strength his  motive has completely changed at this  point katakuri has a direct interest in  luffy actually winning this fight and  proving to him that being yourself is  the right way to go  in a way luffy defeating him would set  him free from the facade that he's built  for himself  [Music]  and so while i believe that luffy fairly  beat category in terms of power and  strength he made it a point to fall on  his back showing luffy his respect for  his growth while at the same time  breaking the biggest aspect of his old  fake persona  now his character has changed completely  from the cold and calculated villain to  a compassionate and honorable antagonist  that has now developed a true liking  towards luffy  and so bringing all of this back to what  we talked about earlier what makes this  fight so different is that luffy is not  liberating someone from the antagonist  but in this case liberates the  antagonist himself  all of this culminates in the  heartwarming scene after the end of  their fight as brulee tends to her  brother's wounds  she knew perfectly well that katakuri  had fallen willingly on his back and  when katakuri asks about luffy brulee  guesses that he would be pleased to know  that luffy has successfully escaped  toddling  katakuri smirks confirming her  assumption and so in the end it was only  brule out of all people who was the only  one to care the most for her brother's  true self and suffering  and bringing this entire theme full  circle it was her that with her mirror  powers enabled his and luffy's change in  the first place  [Music]  as a result i think it's more than fair  to argue that while luffy won the  overall battle katakuri went out of this  fight as a true winner himself having  regained his sense of who he is and  being pulled from his loneliness and  isolation  it sets him up to become relevant once  again in the story and makes him one of  my favorite antagonists in all of one  piece

